  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing configuration so far is config_019 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted; acc 0.639, F1 0.620). All multimodal experiments to date use PCA n2000, a simple linear dimensionality reduction, as the RNA encoder. The image encoder choice (ResNet50 vs ViT-L) shows negligible difference (0.639 vs 0.635), suggesting the RNA representation is the more impactful untested axis. Question: config_031 replaces PCA n2000 with scvi_n200 (a learned deep generative encoder) while holding all other settings at their best-known values (multi-profile, avgpool, weighted, ResNet50). This isolates the effect of a biologically-informed learned RNA representation within the multimodal fusion pipeline. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable extension of the current best configuration, making the result directly interpretable. If scvi_n200 improves performance, it validates investing in learned RNA encoders and opens the scvi multimodal family. If it does not, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects budget toward other axes (e.g., transformer aggregation in multimodal, config_021). Either outcome substantially reduces uncertainty about a core architectural decision under the limited budget."
}

